<title>VENEZUELA: Venezuela and Mexico renew Caribbean oil deal.</title>
<headline>Venezuela and Mexico renew Caribbean oil deal.</headline>
<dateline>CARACAS 1997-08-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>The presidents of Venezuela and Mexico renewed  Friday an oil supply deal with 11 Caribbean and Central American countries,  according to a copy of the agreement sent to Reuters.</p>
<p>The San Jose pact provides for the two oil producers to supply 160,000  barrels per day of crude oil or refined products to the 11 countries  and offer financing for the purchases.</p>
<p>The signatory countries are Barbados, Belize, Costa Rica, El Salvador,  Guatemala, Haiti, Honduras, Jamaica, Nicaragua, Panama, and the Dominican  Republic.</p>
<p>The annual pact was renewed on Friday and takes effect on August 3.  It was first signed in August 1980 in San Jose, Costa Rica.</p>
<p>((-- Tom Ashby, Caracas newsroom, 582 505 2611))</p>
